pyra-backlight (0.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * pyra-idle-dim: turn the keyboard light (*::kbd_backlight LED) off when
    the session goes idle and back on when it wakes, unless it was changed
    meanwhile.
  * pyra-idle-dim: set the keyboard light's level at login, after
    mate-power-manager's reset, from ~/.config/pyra-backlight.conf
    ([keyboard] level = last or 0-100). "last" is kept in
    ~/.local/state/pyra-backlight/kbd-level.
  * pyra-idle-dim.service: ExecReload rereads the config file (SIGHUP).
  * Restart pyra-idle-dim at each MATE login from /etc/xdg/autostart. The
    user unit alone started only with the systemd user manager, so after a
    logout and login with the manager still up (an ssh session open) idle
    dimming was not running.
  * postinst: reload running systemd user managers, which otherwise keep
    the old user unit until reboot.

 -- pyra-backlight maintainers <pyra-backlight@example.invalid>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

pyra-backlight (0.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Applet: drive the keyboard light as an LED (*::kbd_backlight) when the
    kernel declares it that way, in the same nine steps as the stock
    kernel's backlight. The stock kernel's path still works.

 -- pyra-backlight maintainers <pyra-backlight@example.invalid>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0000

